        "type": "text/plain",
        "value": "<div data-rss-type=\"text\">\r\n  <h3>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Pouako \u2013 He Iti N\u0101 M\u014dtai (\u014ctaki)\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h3>\r\n  <h5>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Full-time - permanent role.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </h5>\r\n</div>\r\n<div data-rss-type=\"text\">\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Te W\u0101nanga o Raukawa is seeking an\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           ECE qualified and registered Pouako\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0to join our k\u014dhungahunga,\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           He Iti N\u0101 M\u014dtai\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           , in a\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           full-time, permanent\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0role.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           He Iti N\u0101 M\u014dtai is a kaupapa M\u0101ori centre in \u014ctaki, inspired by our t\u016bpuna\u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           M\u014dtai\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0\u2014 small in stature, yet great in achievement. We offer a spacious learning environment and a strong kaupapa M\u0101ori, te reo M\u0101ori immersion curriculum.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           M\u0101u e mau mai:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            A recognised ECE qualification and current teacher registration\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Strong fluency in written and spoken te reo M\u0101ori\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Experience or knowledge of programme planning, self-review and learning journeys\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Ability to work well in a team, communicate effectively, and open/close the centre\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           E rapu ana m\u0101tou i t\u0113tahi tangata e:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Is passionate about kaupapa M\u0101ori education and tamariki wellbeing\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Is positive, flexible and proactive\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Creates warm, stimulating learning environments\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Ka tukuna e m\u0101tou:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <ul>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Pay parity rates\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            10 days\u2019 sick leave from day one (T&amp;Cs apply)\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Fully funded First Aid\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Ongoing professional development and supportive leadership\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n    <li>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            Mentoring and support for teacher registration (if required)\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </li>\r\n  </ul>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Join a supportive, kaupapa-driven W\u0101nanga and help nurture the next generation of mokopuna.\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           For further information or to apply for this role, please contact:\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           \u00a0\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      \n           Sam Hata, Te Whare Tiaki Rawa\n          \r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           \u012am\u0113ra:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            sam.hata@twor.ac.nz\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <strong>\r\n      \n           Waea:\n          \r\n    </strong>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <span>\r\n        \n            06 3649011 06 3649011\n           \r\n      </span>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n  <p>\r\n    <span>\r\n      <br/>\r\n    </span>\r\n  </p>\r\n</div>"
      }
